{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,260p' '../New project/ai-system/OPERATING_PROTOCOL.md'\nprintf '\\\\n--- PROJECT INDEX matches ---\\\\n'\ngrep -n -i -C 3 'ajamix' '../New project/ai-system/PROJECT_INDEX.md'\nprintf '\\\\n--- project records ---\\\\n'\nfind '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix' -maxdepth 2 -type f -print | sort\nprintf '\\\\n--- session log tail ---\\\\n'\ntail -120 '../New project/ai-system/SESSION_LOG.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Shared AI Operating Protocol\n\nThis workspace uses `ai-system/` as the shared operating record for Claude Code and Codex. Chat history is not the source of truth for serious project work. The source of truth is the project record in this folder plus the user's latest instruction.\n\nCanonical workspace root:\n\n```text\n/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/New project\n```\n\nIf an agent sees or creates `/Users/muhammadbamalli/ai-system`, treat it as a mistaken home-directory duplicate for this workspace unless the user explicitly says otherwise. Do not use the home-directory duplicate as the source of truth for work in this project.\n\n## Core Rule\n\nClaude Code and Codex should not rely on separate chat histories. For serious project work, both must read the shared `ai-system` records before planning, record execution after work, and prepare handoff notes when context or tokens are getting low.\n\n## Start-of-Work Checklist\n\nBefore meaningful work:\n\n1. Read this file.\n2. Resolve the project name or alias in `ai-system/PROJECT_INDEX.md`.\n3. Read the project's required records:\n   - `PROJECT_BRIEF.md`\n   - `PROJECT_PLAN.md`\n   - `CURRENT_STATE.md`\n   - `ACTIVE_TASK.md`\n   - latest entry in `SESSION_NOTES.md` or `SESSION_LOG.md`\n4. Check for conflicts between:\n   - the user's current chat instruction,\n   - the project brief,\n   - the current plan,\n   - the current state,\n   - the active task,\n   - any decision log entries.\n5. Before executing, tell the user:\n   - identified project,\n   - current stage,\n   - next step.\n\nIf required records do not exist yet, create the missing project folder and starter records before doing major work.\n\n## Conflict Rule\n\nThe user's latest instruction controls the current session, but durable project files control standing context. If they conflict:\n\n1. Do not silently overwrite the durable record.\n2. Name the conflict briefly.\n3. Ask for confirmation if the conflict changes scope, legal/evidentiary posture, filing strategy, architecture, data handling, or deliverable format.\n4. If the user confirms a change, update the relevant project files after the work.\n\n## Conversational Resume Commands\n\nFor commands such as \"continue the Konfirmata task Claude was doing at 8pm\":\n\n1. Resolve \"Konfirmata\" through `PROJECT_INDEX.md`.\n2. Search `SESSION_LOG.md` and the project `SESSION_NOTES.md` for the nearest timestamp or time reference.\n3. Read the linked or implied `ACTIVE_TASK.md`, `CURRENT_STATE.md`, and recent task file.\n4. Tell the user what was found, the inferred next step, and any uncertainty.\n5. Continue only after the resume target is clear enough to avoid damaging existing work.\n\n## Project Record Structure\n\nEach project should live under:\n\n```text\nai-system/projects/<project-id>/\n```\n\nRecommended files:\n\n```text\nPROJECT_BRIEF.md\nPROJECT_PLAN.md\nCURRENT_STATE.md\nACTIVE_TASK.md\nDECISIONS.md\nSESSION_NOTES.md\ntasks/\nhandoffs/\n```\n\nUse stable project IDs in lowercase kebab case, for example `konfirmata-niw` or `confirma-site`.\n\nTo onboard a new project, copy `ai-system/projects/_TEMPLATE/` to `ai-system/projects/<project-id>/`, then fill the records from authoritative workspace files before executing substantive work.\n\n## Project Plans With Stages\n\n`PROJECT_PLAN.md` should contain:\n\n- objective,\n- stages,\n- current stage,\n- stage exit criteria,\n- known blockers,\n- next planned task.\n\nStages should be explicit enough that another model can resume without guessing.\n\n## Current State Tracking\n\n`CURRENT_STATE.md` should answer:\n\n- What is true now?\n- What files or artifacts are authoritative?\n- What is in progress?\n- What is blocked or risky?\n- What should happen next?\n\nUpdate it after medium, major, or strategic work.\n\n## Task Execution Records\n\nFor major tasks, create or update a task file under:\n\n```text\nai-system/projects/<project-id>/tasks/YYYY-MM-DD-short-task-name.md\n```\n\nEach task file should include:\n\n- request,\n- starting context,\n- actions taken,\n- files touched,\n- verification performed,\n- result,\n- remaining work.\n\n## Decision Logs\n\n`DECISIONS.md` records project decisions that should survive chat context. Use this format:\n\n```text\n## YYYY-MM-DD - Decision Title\n\n- Decision:\n- Reason:\n- Evidence or source:\n- Impact:\n- Revisit if:\n```\n\nRecord decisions when work changes strategy, scope, claim boundaries, architecture, source hierarchy, data model, or operating assumptions.\n\n## Session Notes\n\n`SESSION_LOG.md` is the cross-project index of meaningful sessions. Project-specific `SESSION_NOTES.md` files hold more detail.\n\nEvery meaningful session note should include:\n\n- timestamp with timezone,\n- model or tool if known,\n- project,\n- user request,\n- work completed,\n- files touched,\n- verification,\n- next step.\n\n## Tiered Update Rule\n\nUse the lightest durable update that preserves continuity:\n\n- Tiny task: session note only.\n- Medium task: current state + session note.\n- Major task: current state + task file + session note + decisions when applicable.\n- Strategic change: also update project plan and project brief.\n\nIf unsure, treat the work as medium.\n\n## Low-Token Handoff Rule\n\nWhen context or tokens are getting low:\n\n1. Stop starting new substantive work.\n2. Create a handoff note under:\n\n```text\nai-system/projects/<project-id>/handoffs/YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM-handoff.md\n```\n\n3. Include:\n   - current objective,\n   - exact current stage,\n   - latest user instruction,\n   - files read,\n   - files changed,\n   - commands run,\n   - decisions made,\n   - unresolved questions,\n   - next safe action.\n4. Add a short pointer to `SESSION_LOG.md`.\n\n## End-of-Work Checklist\n\nAfter meaningful work:\n\n1. Apply the tiered update rule.\n2. Record verification and remaining risk.\n3. If files changed, make sure the session note names them.\n4. If the next model needs context, write a handoff or clear next-step note.\n\n--- PROJECT INDEX matches ---\n78-  - `ereva/`\n79-- Notes: PRD v2 and TAS v2 are authoritative. Never override `[DECIDED]` items; use mock adapters for undecided providers until human decisions are made.\n80-\n81:### AJAMIX\n82-\n83:- Project ID: `ajamix`\n84:- Folder: `ai-system/projects/ajamix/`\n85:- Aliases: `AJAMIX`, `ajamix`, `MATH-P3-Pilot`, `p3-maths`, `M1`\n86-- Existing workspace anchors:\n87:  - `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix`\n88-- Notes: For MATH-P3-Pilot M1, only `p3-maths-01..06` are authorized. Do not scale to `p3-maths-07` or beyond before Architect review. Do not touch git or runtime files unless a later user instruction explicitly changes scope.\n89-\n90-### Invention Engine (Forge)\n\n--- project records ---\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/ACTIVE_TASK.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/CURRENT_STATE.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/DECISIONS.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_BRIEF.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_PLAN.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/SESSION_NOTES.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/handoffs/2026-07-07-2237-handoff.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/handoffs/2026-07-23-2222-handoff.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-04-math-p3-pilot-m1.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-05-math-p3-m2-source-draft.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects