d\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-26-slice-21-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-26-slice-21.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-V01-V03-audio-adaptation-packet.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-pre-segments-content-389.json\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-21-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-21.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-22-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-22-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-22-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-22.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-23-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-23-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-23-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-23.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-24-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-24-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-24-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-24.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-26-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-26-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-26-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-26.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-27-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-27-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-27-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-27.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-28-brief.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-28-final-message.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-28-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-27-slice-28.jsonl\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/image-manifest-genuine-content-final-message.txt\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/image-manifest-genuine-content-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/p1-bsci-redundancy-last-message.txt\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/p1-bsci-redundancy-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/p5-bsci-builder-report.md\n../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/p5-bsci-output-last-message.txt\n\n--- session log tail ---\n  All independently verified by Claude: checksums, `content.json` untouched, `validate-content.mjs` clean\n  at 369 modules. A postflight FAIL on the promotion slice was investigated and confirmed to be a false\n  positive (one-shot script's own safety guard correctly refusing a second run, not a real failure) — see\n  the handoff for detail, worth remembering for future non-idempotent-script slices.\n- Started the audio track same day: recording packages for all 359 modules\n  (`tools/audio-pipeline/recording-packages/`), `ffmpeg`/`ffprobe` installed (Homebrew), delivery-QA\n  tooling built and verified end-to-end against real placeholder MP3s. Recording itself and TIMSAN review\n  remain external/human steps.\n- Full detail: `ai-system/projects/ajamix/handoffs/2026-07-23-2222-handoff.md`.\n\n## 2026-07-25 — Ajamix: Critical Thinking (`Tunani da Tantancewa`) opened; M1 source-only pilot built and verified\n\n- Audio track still blocked on external recording delivery; opened a new adult-track subject instead.\n- Claude self-critiqued its own proposed curriculum and found real defects (unassessable Philosophy modules\n  under the one-correct-answer quiz schema, a `qadar` sensitivity landmine, unchecked overlap with `V04`/`V05`/\n  `V06`/`V10` and Social Studies civics). Both 10-module lists rebuilt under assessability + no-doctrine +\n  no-overlap rules. Philosophy deliberately deferred.\n- Corpus evidence overturned the provisional subject name: `X Mai Zurfi` is an existing module-title idiom\n  (\"deeper study of X\"), so `Tunani Mai Zurfi` was rejected. Muhammad locked `Tunani da Tantancewa`.\n- Fixed stale `PROJECT_PLAN.md` stage 16 (Social Studies marked ACTIVE though merged 2026-07-17).\n- M1 pilot (CT01-CT03) built via dispatch-codex slice `2026-07-25-slice-01`, source-only, `app/content.json`\n  untouched (checksum-verified). Gate script negative-tested with 6 injected defects, all caught. Status:\n  awaiting Muhammad's Hausa/content approval. Two open items: apostrophe convention vs the vocational track,\n  and a null-Ajami-vs-validator blocker that must be resolved before this subject can ever merge.\n\n## 2026-07-25 (part 2) — Ajamix: CT M1 corrected twice, now HUMAN-REVIEW READY\n\n- Two correction slices after Muhammad's reviews: slice-02 (four content rulings + Ajami-aware validator\n  with 6 regression cases) and slice-03 (final two wording fixes, Luna/medium). Both process failures from\n  slice-01 repaired and verified — separate report paths, parser-verified scope globs.\n- `validate-content.mjs` is now conditional on `ajami_validated`, which unblocks null-Ajami adult-track\n  modules; live 369 corpus still passes, scratch temp-merge validates at 372.\n- Two defects were caught by reading rather than by any gate (a glossary/example duplication and a missing\n  copula) — both fixed in slice-03. Standing lesson reconfirmed: \"all gates pass\" ≠ \"brief satisfied.\"\n- Status: `Tunani da Tantancewa M1: HUMAN-REVIEW READY`. Binding ruling: do not integrate CT01-CT03\n  separately; author CT04-CT10 source-only next and integrate all ten as one chain with CT10 as sole leaf.\n\n## 2026-07-26 — Codex orchestration tooling: three postmortem fixes from ajamix slice-17\n\nTriggered by the Critical Thinking (CT) guarded-merge dispatch for ajamix (slice-17): the dispatch omitted\n`--add-dir` for a sibling checkout a merge script needed to write its backup to, Codex's own sandboxed\nattempt correctly failed with `EPERM` and declined to report success, but postflight's independent re-run\nof the acceptance-gate command (from an unrestricted shell) then performed the actual live 379->389 merge as\na side effect of \"verification\" — outside Codex's reviewed turn. The overall dispatch verdict showed FAIL,\nbut only from an unrelated scope-fence false positive (it diffed the whole working tree vs `HEAD`, catching\nthis repo's long-standing uncommitted drift from weeks earlier, not anything the slice touched). The\nintegration itself was independently re-verified byte-for-byte after the fact and confirmed correct — see\n`projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-26-slice-17-report.md` — but the tooling gaps that produced this confusing\noutcome were fixed directly (per Muhammad's explicit choice, not dispatched to Codex, given the recursive\nrisk of using the unfixed script to deploy its own successor):\n\n1. **`Add-dir required:` brief field** — `codex-dispatch.sh` now hard-aborts *before* dispatching if the\n   brief declares a write path outside `--repo` that isn't covered by any `--add-dir`, instead of finding\n   out via `EPERM` mid-dispatch. Optional field, WARN (not abort) if absent, for backward compatibility.\n2. **`--verify-cmd-mutating`** — `codex-postflight.sh` now snapshots the repo's dirty/untracked\n   content-hash manifest before and after re-running `--verify-cmd`; if it changed and this flag wasn't\n   passed, postflight hard-fails instead of silently accepting a live write performed by a \"verification\"\n   step.\n3. **Snapshot-scoped `Scope globs:` check** — `codex-dispatch.sh` now dumps a path+content-hash manifest of\n   the repo's dirty/untracked state immediately before dispatching (new `scripts/lib/status-manifest.py`)\n   and passes it to postflight via `--pre-status`. The scope-fence check diffs against that snapshot instead\n   of the whole working tree vs `HEAD`, so pre-existing uncommitted drift no longer gets misattributed to\n   the current slice. Falls back to the old whole-tree method (WARN, not hard fail) if `--pre-status` is\n   omitted.\n\nAll three fixes were tested against reconstructions of the exact slice-17 failure mode in a disposable throwaway\ngit repo (not ajamix) before being trusted: confirmed the old scope-fence bug is real and reproducible without\n`--pre-status`, confirmed it's fixed with `--pre-status`, confirmed a mutating `--verify-cmd` now hard-fails\nwithout acknowledgment and passes cleanly with it, and confirmed a read-only `--verify-cmd` is unaffected.\nAlso confirmed (and fixed) a `set -u`/empty-array bash 3.2 crash in the new add-dir-check loop, mirroring a\npreviously-documented gotcha with the same failure class elsewhere in this script. `CODEX_ORCHESTRATION.md`\nupdated with the new brief field, the new flag, and a postmortem note in the canonical-invocation section.\nNo curriculum content, no other project's scripts, and no git operations were touched by this work.\n## 2026-07-27 — Nightbook session gate moved to Home\n\n- Identified Nightbook and fixed the morning/night session readiness UX.\n- Home now names Wheel areas without an active planner, disables session entry, and\n  links directly to Goals; SessionPlayer's guard remains as fallback.\n- Verified 99 tests, production build, Vercel READY deployment\n  `dpl_J5tx9jsywmYKrgfLD6vyAvodL3ai`, and canonical asset copy.\n## 2026-07-27 — Nightbook fresh-storage sync restore\n\n- Fixed startup ordering so an existing sync session is pulled before the onboarding\n  decision after local database storage is cleared.\n- Recorded limitation: clearing localStorage also removes the session token, requiring\n  sign-in again before remote restore.\n## 2026-07-27 — Nightbook session goal titles and description editing\n\n- Session planner steps now show the goal title and provide an Edit description\n  action that opens the existing Goal Editor for that goal.\n- Deployment is pending because this environment cannot write the project's build\n  temp files.\n\n## 2026-07-28 — Standalone PPTX-to-PDF conversion\n\n- Converted `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Downloads/Lubabatu Muhammad A.pptx` directly\n  to `output/pdf/Lubabatu Muhammad A.pdf` without editing the source deck.\n- Verified 24 source slides became 24 PDF pages at the original 16:9 dimensions\n  (960 x 540 points), and visually reviewed the full-deck montage plus the densest\n  table and reference pages.\n- Source presentation remains unchanged. No further work is required.\n\n## 2026-07-28 01:18 EDT — Islamic Essentials (Sirāj) Stage 0 + Stage 1 complete\n\n- Onboarded the new `islamic-essentials` project from the attached master build\n  brief and created the isolated Vite + strict TypeScript app at\n  `islamic-essentials/`.\n- Completed Stage 0 and the playable Tawḥīd in Everyday Life vertical slice:\n  two adaptive presentations from one shared topic, strong acceleration,\n  respectful remediation, application, six vocabulary items, deterministic\n  mastery, local persistence, real-life mission, delayed-review record, and\n  parent card.\n- Content is source-linked but remains `household_review_required`; no detailed\n  Māliki/Tijānī assumptions, recitation functionality, backend, analytics, or\n  productization were added.\n- Verification PASS: 16 tests, strict production build, both end-to-end routes,\n  reload persistence, responsive layouts, zero browser errors, no serious or\n  critical axe findings, visual QA across 8 screens, and 0 npm vulnerabilities.\n- Postflight: `islamic-essentials/docs/STAGE_1_POSTFLIGHT.md`.\n- Next gate: owner tests with both children and complete