{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"for task_path in '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_BRIEF.md' '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_PLAN.md' '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/CURRENT_STATE.md' '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/ACTIVE_TASK.md'; do printf '\\\\n===== %s =====\\\\n' \\\"\"'$task_path\"; sed -n '\"'1,260p' \\\"\"'$task_path\"; done\nprintf '\"'\\\\n===== SESSION NOTES (tail) =====\\\\n'\ntail -180 '../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/SESSION_NOTES.md'\"","aggregated_output":"\n===== ../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_BRIEF.md =====\n# Project Brief: AJAMIX\n\n## Objective\n\nAJAMIX is an offline-first education app with Hausa/Ajami learning content. Mathematics P3-P6 and Basic Science P3-P6 are complete in the live 309-module app. **Current objective: review the Social Studies P3 M2 source-only completion batch (`p3-socs-07..15`) and rule on the new terminology questions before M3**, then continue the subject one grade band at a time through the same source-review and guarded-merge discipline.\n\nThe completed P6 Basic Science band used the detailed NERDC Primary 6 Basic Science and Basic Technology curriculum as its backbone, enriched—not replaced—by Cambridge Primary Science and England upper-KS2 practices. Its governing map is `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/docs/BSCI-P6-HYBRID-CANONICAL-MAP.md` and its guarded merge closure is recorded in `tasks/2026-07-13-p6-bsci-guarded-merge-report.md`.\n\nP6 Basic Science (`p6-bsci-01..15`) is approved, merged, idempotency-proven, and validator-green at 309 total modules. Image generation remains paused by the user's 2026-07-13 direction.\n\n**Current queue:**\n1. **Social Studies P3-P6** (\"basic humanities\") — this is NOT a new subject; it is the content for the already-planned Social Studies P3-P6 gap. The architect brief and provisional 60-row M0 matrix are approved as the working basis. M1 source-only pilot (`p3-socs-01..06`) is approved, patched, and verified. M2 (`p3-socs-07..15`) is built and independently verified, awaiting Muhammad's Hausa/content review and terminology rulings before M3.\n2. **Philosophy and Critical Thinking** — two new, SEPARATE adult-track subjects, each mirroring the existing `Vocational Skills` schema exactly (rich lesson-array format, not the lighter P3-P6 schema), roughly 10 modules each. Queued behind both Basic Science and Social Studies P3-P6. Hausa subject names, topic anchors, and exact module counts are not yet decided — needs a dedicated architect brief and the user's terminology ruling before any build starts.\n\nSee `PROJECT_PLAN.md` Stages 15-17 for full detail on all three queued/in-flight items.\n\nPrior objective (complete, kept for history): MATH-P6 M5 — draft Primary 6 Mathematics modules, `p6-maths-01` through `p6-maths-24`. Completed and merged 2026-07-07.\n\n## Scope\n\n- M1 approved and merged: `p3-maths-01..06` in `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/app/content.json`.\n- M2 approved and merged: `p3-maths-07..24` merged into `app/content.json`, bringing the count from 148 to 166 modules.\n- M3 approved and merged: `p4-maths-01..24` merged into `app/content.json`, bringing the count from 166 to 190 modules.\n- M4 approved and merged: `p5-maths-01..24` merged into `app/content.json`, bringing the count from 190 to 214 modules (merged and closed 2026-07-06, verified idempotent).\n- P6 Mathematics and P6 Basic Science are complete and merged.\n- Current development scope is Social Studies P3-P6 M2 review: `p3-socs-07..15` exists source-only and must be reviewed before M3 source authoring.\n- Continue source-only candidate work, explicit Hausa/content rulings, independent gates, and controlled idempotent merges.\n- Do not resume image generation unless the user explicitly reopens that workstream.\n\n## Audience Or User\n\nPrimary 3–6 learners using AJAMIX Hausa/Ajami educational content, with separate adult-track content where explicitly planned.\n\n## Authoritative Files And Sources\n\n- Repository: `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix`\n- M1 batch (merged): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p3-batch/p3-maths-pilot.json`\n- M2 source (merged): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p3-batch/p3-maths-m2.json`\n- M3 source (merged): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p4-batch/p4-maths.json`\n- M4 source (merged): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p5-batch/p5-maths.json`\n- M4 merge script pattern (template for M5): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p5-batch/merge-p5-maths.mjs`\n- M5 source draft (in progress): `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/tools/p6-batch/p6-maths.json`\n- Schema contract: `/Users/muhammadbamalli/Documents/ajamix/docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-MATH-P3-P6.md` §5 (also §4 for P6 indicative topic anchors, §7 for milestone M5 = P6 complete, M6 = full P3-P6 band merged)\n\n## Constraints And Claim Boundaries\n\n- Do not touch git.\n- Do not modify engine or runtime files.\n- Do not manually edit `app/content.json`; future merge must use a controlled script.\n- Do not write outside `tools/p6-batch/` for M5 work.\n- Preserve existing modules, grade bands, glossary, and activities.\n- M5 source modules must follow the M1-M4 schema contract (`docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-MATH-P3-P6.md` §5).\n- All Ajami fields remain `null`; `ajami_validated: false`.\n- Exactly 2 micro-pauses and exactly 5 parameterized quiz questions per module.\n- Audio pause questions must match `microPauses[].questionHa` exactly.\n- Quiz outputs must remain non-negative and distinct across random instances.\n- Hausa corrections after approval must be literal patches only.\n- **Every quiz formula beyond direct arithmetic must be brute-force-verified against ground truth** — the standard formula-safety harness only checks non-negativity/distinctness, not real mathematical correctness. This was the single most consequential lesson of M4 (the original LCM formulas in P5 Slice 1 passed the harness but were mathematically wrong for many sampled values).\n- Never reuse the same variable for two independent roles in a quiz template in a way that makes the answer invariant (the M3 Slice-4 defect).\n- A single-pass regex terminology substitution is not enough — always follow with a case-insensitive re-scan of the full patched scope (the M4 Slice-2 lesson: mixed-case sentence-initial variants get missed).\n- Watch for circular definitions (\"X ana kiran ta X\") and duplicated-word typos (\"X X\") after any substitution or new content generation.\n- Use `×` in learner-facing `templateHa` text; keep `*` only in `answerFormula`/`distractorFormulas`.\n- Hausa gender agreement: `lambar`/`lamba`-based nouns take `wace`, not `wane`.\n- Do not trust Codex's self-reported \"full module content\" in its report as complete — one M4 slice's report was truncated to 1 of 6 modules; always read the live source file directly for verification and for presenting content to the user.\n- Codex delegation must go through the `dispatch-codex` skill (per `CLAUDE.md`), with full M0 preflight per `ai-system/CODEX_ORCHESTRATION.md`.\n- Scope-safety verification for protected runtime files should prefer content checksums (e.g. `shasum -a 256`) over modification timestamps alone, since `git status`/`git diff` are unreliable (hang unpredictably) in this repo — a process note added after M4's closure.\n\n## Locked P3/P4/P5 House-Standard Terminology (carry forward; do not respell)\n\n- P3/P4: `desimal`, `perimita`, `siffar rektangul`/`rektangul`, `goma-goma`, `ɗari-ɗari`, `yanki` (area), `kusurwa madaidaiciya` (right angle).\n- P5: LCM/HCF (`mafi ƙaramin ninki na gari`, `ninki na gari`/`ninkaye na gari`, `mafi girman mai raba gari`, `mai raba gari`/`masu raba gari`); fractions (`lambar sama`, `lambar ƙasa`, `kashi masu ƙima ɗaya`, `lambar ƙasa ta gari`, `lambobin ƙasa na gari`, `ninkawa a giciye`, `kashi`); decimals/percentages (`desimal`, `alamar desimal`, `matsayi na goma-goma`, `matsayi na ɗari-ɗari`, `kashi cikin ɗari`, `percent`); ratio/geometry/statistics (`rasiyo`, `daidaiton rabo`, `ɓangare`/`ɓangarori`, `haɗaɗɗiyar siffa`/`haɗaɗɗun siffofi`, `ma'aunin kusurwa`, `digiri`, `ƙaramar kusurwa`, `babbar kusurwa`, `matsakaici`, `matsalolin kalma masu haɗa ayyuka`).\n- P6 will introduce new terms (algebra/unknowns, volume, probability, mastery-level operation vocabulary) requiring their own Hausa house-standard rulings from the user during slice review — do not assume any P6-specific term is locked until ruled on.\n\n## Known Risks\n\n- M5 (P6 Mathematics) has not yet been built; topic anchors are indicative only per the architect brief §4 and need refinement against the actual NERDC BEC P6 syllabus, same caveat as every prior band.\n- New Hausa vocabulary for P6 (algebra/unknown, volume, probability, etc.) is not yet terminology-locked; expect new house-standard rulings during slice review.\n- P6's topic-anchor list is dense (9 clusters: numbers/operations mastery, fractions/decimals/percentages conversions, ratio/proportion, simple algebra, area/perimeter/volume, angles in shapes, data/probability, revision-bridge to JSS1) across only 4 slices of 6 — expect at least one slice (likely the final one) to need topic compression, same as M4 Slice 4.\n- The M5 merge (214 → 238) will not run until all four slices are Hausa/content-approved; requires a controlled script mirroring `merge-p5-maths.mjs`, hard count assertion, and idempotency proof.\n- The AJAMIX repo had pre-existing unrelated modified and untracked files during M1; do not inspect or touch git unless explicitly authorized. `git status`/`git diff` have also proven unreliable (hang unpredictably) throughout M4 — route around via direct file inspection rather than forcing retries.\n- **ai-system durable records for this project drifted stale at points in 2026-07 prior to a mid-M4 catch-up pass** (see `DECISIONS.md`); the underlying write-back gap is tracked as a standing setup issue in `~/.claude/reflection-notes.md` item #5.\n\n## Last Updated\n\n2026-07-16\n\n===== ../New project/ai-system/projects/ajamix/PROJECT_PLAN.md =====\n# Project Plan: AJAMIX\n\n## Objective\n\nMathematics P3-P6 (prior objective, COMPLETE — see Stages 1-13 below): safely complete P3, P4, P5, and P6 Mathematics content for AJAMIX while preserving the content-only workflow, source review gates, and controlled merge discipline.\n\n**Current objective: adult-track curriculum completion under the same source-review, terminology-lock, and guarded-merge discipline.** Social Studies P3-P6 is complete; Falsafa M1 is now live; `Tunani da Tantancewa` remains a separate source-only subject pending its own authorization.\n\n## Current Stage\n\nFalsafa M1 guarded integration is complete: `FL01..FL10` are live in `app/content.json` at 379 modules (369 -> 379), with an idempotency-proven merger and rollback backup at `ai-system/projects/ajamix/tasks/2026-07-25-pre-falsafa-merge-content-369.json`. Mathematics P3-P6, Basic Science P3-P6, and Social Studies P3-P6 are also complete in the live app. No next subject action is authorized by this slice.\n\n## Stages\n\n1. M1 completion\n   - Goal: Merge and approve `p3-maths-01..06`.\n   - Exit criteria: App content count 148, technical gates green, Hausa/content gate approved.\n   - Status: Complete.\n\n2. M2 source draft\n   - Goal: Create `tools/p3-batch/p3-maths-m2.json` with exactly 18 modules, `p3-maths-07..24`.\n   - Exit criteria: Source JSON parses, IDs/module numbers are exact, schema/micro-pauses/quiz counts pass, preliminary formulas pass, hook-lint passes.\n   - Status: Complete.\n\n3. M2 slice review\n   - Goal: User/Foreman review the source in three slices: `07..12`, `13..18`, and `19..24`.\n   - Exit criteria: All requested Hausa/content corrections are literal-patched into the source draft and source checks remain green.\n   - Status: Complete. All three slices approved.\n\n4. M2 controlled merge\n   - Goal: After source approval, merge only `p3-maths-07..24` into `app/content.json` with an idempotent script.\n   - Exit criteria: Count moves from 148 to 166, existing IDs are preserved, JSON reparses, idempotency is proven, and app validator/formula/hook checks pass.\n   - Status: Complete. `app/content.json` verified at 166 modules (2026-07-06).\n\n5. M3 (P4 Mathematics) source draft\n   - Goal: Create `tools/p4-batch/p4-maths.json` with 24 modules, `p4-maths-01..24`.\n   - Exit criteria: Source JSON parses, IDs/module numbers exact, schema/micro-pause/quiz counts pass, formula harness passes, hook-lint passes.\n   - Status: Complete. 24 of 24 modules built and verified.\n\n6. M3 slice review\n   - Goal: User/Foreman review the source in four slices: `01..06`, `07..12`, `13..18`, `19..24` (final).\n   - Exit criteria: All requested Hausa/content corrections are literal-patched and source checks remain green; terminology stays consistent with the locked P4 house standard.\n   - Status: Complete. All four slices approved. Slice 4 approval was conditional on a literal patch to `p4-maths-20` Q2 (fixed a same-variable division defect); patch applied 2026-07-06 and all gates re-passed.\n\n7. M3 controlled merge\n   - Goal: After all four slices are approved, merge `p4-maths-01..24` into `app/content.json` with an idempotent script mirroring `merge-p3-maths-pilot.mjs`.\n   - Exit criteria: Count moves from 166 to 190, existing IDs preserved, JSON reparses, idempotency proven, app validator/formula/hook checks pass.\n   - Status: Complete. Merge run 2026-07-06 with explicit user go-ahead. `app/content.json` verified at 190 modules. Idempotency proven (second run no-op). `validate-content.mjs`, `check-p4-maths-formulas.mjs`, `check-p4-maths-structure.mjs`, and `hook-lint.mjs` all pass (0 errors; 7 pre-existing warnings on an unrelated M1/M2 module, not a regression).\n\n8. M4 (P5 Mathematics) source draft\n   - Goal: Create `tools/p5-batch/p5-maths.json` with 24 modules, `p5-maths-01..24`, in four slices of 6 (`01..06`, `07..12`, `13..18`, `19..24`), mirroring the M3 process.\n   - Topic anchors (indicative, per `docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-MATH-P3-P6.md` §4, refine against actual NERDC BEC P5 syllabus): numbers to 100,000; LCM & HCF; fraction operations (add/subtract unlike denominators); decimal operations; intro percentages; ratio & proportion (intro); area & perimeter (composite shapes); angles (types, measuring); average/mean (intro); word problems combining operations; `p5-maths-24` as a P5 revision module bridging to P6 (same pattern as `p3-maths-24`/`p4-maths-24`).\n   - Exit criteria per slice: source JSON parses, IDs/module numbers exact, schema/micro-pause/quiz counts pass, formula harness passes, hook-lint passes, no same-variable-reuse defects (per the M3 Slice-4 lesson).\n   - Status: All 4 slices (`p5-maths-01..24`) built and gates independently verified — M4 source draft is complete (24 of 24 modules). Slice 4 was clean on first pass (no defects found, unlike every prior slice).\n\n9. M4 slice review\n   - Goal: User/Foreman review the source in four slices, same discipline as M2/M3.\n   - Exit criteria: All requested Hausa/content corrections are literal-patched and source checks remain green; new P5 terminology gets explicit house-standard rulings from the user.\n   - Status: Complete. All four slices approved 2026-07-06. Slice 4 approved after five specific confirmations checked against the live text (rasiyo relational framing, angle-type degree bounds, protractor explanation, no new synonyms for locked terms).\n\n10. M4 controlled merge\n    - Goal: After all four slices are approved, merge `p5-maths-01..24` into `app/content.json` with an idempotent script mirroring `merge-p4-maths.mjs`.\n    - Exit criteria: Count moves from 190 to 214, existing IDs preserved, JSON reparses, idempotency proven, app validator/formula/hook checks pass.\n    - Status: Complete. Merge run 2026-