26-07-07 (terminology locked: `miliyan ɗaya`/`miliyan`, `dubu ɗari`, `jadawalin matsayi`, `kimantawa`/`kiyasta`, `zagaye lamba`, `goma/dubu/dubu goma mafi kusa`, `ka ɗaga`). Slice 2 approved 2026-07-07 after one house-style wording patch (`matsalolin kalmomi` → `matsalolin kalma`, P5 consistency); terminology locked: `desimal mai ƙarewa`, `nau'i`, `sauyin nau'i`, `adadin farko`, `matsalolin kalma`. Slice 3 approved 2026-07-07 after a word-count top-up patch and a `ma'auni` disambiguation patch (`ma'aunin lissafi` for \"equation\" in `p6-maths-15/16`, keeping generic `ma'auni` for \"rate/factor/dimension\" elsewhere); terminology locked: `algebra`, `canji`, `ma'aunin lissafi`, `kuboid`, `girma`, `tsayi`, `cubic unit`. Slice 4 (FINAL) approved 2026-07-07 after a `marasa ja`→`ba ja ba` consistency patch and a `kididdiga`→`ƙididdiga` hooked-letter fix; terminology locked: `alwatika`, `siffa mai gefe huɗu`, `yiwuwar faruwa`, `sakamakon zaɓe`, `ƙididdiga`, `ba ja ba`. This slice's build also added the previously-missing word-count assertion to `check-p6-maths-structure.mjs`, retroactively covering all 24 modules.\n\n13. M5 controlled merge\n    - Goal: After all four slices are approved, merge `p6-maths-01..24` into `app/content.json` with an idempotent script mirroring `merge-p5-maths.mjs`.\n    - Exit criteria: Count moves from 214 to 238, existing IDs preserved, JSON reparses, idempotency proven, app validator/formula/hook checks pass. Scope-safety verification should use content checksums (`shasum -a 256`) for protected runtime files, not mtimes alone (process note from M4 closure).\n    - Status: COMPLETE. Merge run 2026-07-07 with explicit user go-ahead (script prepared and presented first, per the established M4 two-step pattern). `app/content.json` verified at 238 modules. Idempotency proven (second run correctly no-op'd). `app/tools/validate-content.mjs`, `check-p6-maths-formulas.mjs`, `check-p6-maths-structure.mjs`, and `hook-lint.mjs` (both source and merged) all pass — merged content shows the same 7 pre-existing (non-regression) warnings documented since the M3 merge. Scope safety confirmed via direct file inspection and content checksums (`git status` hung again, worked around per standing process note).\n\n14. Basic Science P3-P6 brief\n    - Goal: Draft `docs/ARCHITECT-BRIEF-BSCI-P3-P6.md` mirroring the Math brief's structure — schema contract, topic anchors per band, milestone plan, terminology carryover, standing lessons.\n    - Exit criteria: Brief drafted, synced to `~/Downloads/`, ai-system records updated, presented for explicit user approval.\n    - Status: Complete. Brief drafted, approved, and superseded by build progress (see Stage 15) — this project's records were reconciled 2026-07-07 in a parallel session to reflect that approval and build had already progressed past this stage.\n\n15. Basic Science P3-Pilot (M1 of Basic Science P3-P6)\n    - Goal: Build `tools/p3-batch/p3-bsci.json` (6 modules, `p3-bsci-01..06`) via `dispatch-codex`, same discipline as every Math arc milestone.\n    - Exit criteria: Source JSON parses, schema/gate checks pass, independently re-verified by Claude, Hausa/content reviewed (two rounds: `ƙarfi`→`abu mai tauri`, `kitchen`→`wurin dafa abinci`, `fitar da iri`→`samar da iri`), merged into `app/content.json` with idempotency proof and full validation.\n    - Status: COMPLETE. Merged 2026-07-09. Count moved 238→244.\n\n16. Basic Science P3 M2 (complete P3 band to 15/15)\n    - Goal: Build `tools/p3-batch/p3-bsci-m2.json` (9 modules, `p3-bsci-07..15`) via `dispatch-codex`.\n    - Exit criteria: Same as M1 — gates green, Hausa/content reviewed (rulings: `nauyi`/`giram`/`kilogiram` locked, `iska mai ƙarfi` confirmed, traditional-vs-modern-tech confirmed as Basic Science, `p3-bsci-13` first-aid tone patched for adult-supervision framing), merged with idempotency proof and full validation.\n    - Status: COMPLETE. Merged 2026-07-10 with an outside-repo pre-merge audit snapshot (244-mod